# Files that must never be uploaded as public static assets.
#
# This is the root of the repository, so the assets directory IS the working
# tree. Without this file wrangler uploads everything in it, and everything in
# it becomes a public URL. That is not theoretical: before this file existed,
# https://mayongbesttantrik.com/.git/config returned 200 and served the
# repository's remote URL to anyone who asked, along with /.git/index,
# /.git/logs/HEAD, /build.js and every file under /content.
#
# Syntax is gitignore's. Patterns are anchored to the root of the assets
# directory, so /*.js matches the build scripts at the top level while leaving
# the site's own js/ directory alone - that one is real, referenced by every
# page, and must be served.

# Version control. .git/index lists every path in the working tree and
# .git/logs/HEAD records every commit ref that has ever been checked out.
/.git/

# Build tooling and page source. Not secret, but none of it is meant to be
# fetched by a visitor or a crawler, and /content/en.js is the entire copy of
# the site in one request.
/*.js
/content/
/.kilo/
/issues/

# The lastmod ledger is build state, not site content. The dates it produces
# are already published in sitemap.xml.
/.lastmod.json

# Repo and deploy config. worker.js and wrangler.jsonc are read by wrangler at
# deploy time and must not be served.
/.gitignore
/.assetsignore
/wrangler.jsonc
/assetsignore

# Tooling that has no business being public.
/*.ps1
/*.md
/node_modules/
/.wrangler/
